sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor D as Demo presenter
    participant C as HTML channel test interface
    participant A as HTTP API authentication
    participant P as Processor and channel ACL
    participant DB as DynamoDB business and event source
    participant S as Simulated switch/network
    participant I as Simulated issuer
    participant T as ADOT technical telemetry
    Note over D,A: One demo JWT principal, existing issuer/session checks and backend service IAM remain distinct
    D->>C: Explicitly submit a synthetic POS authorization
    C->>A: HTTP request using current authenticated demo session
    A->>A: Validate JWT and current mandate
    break Authentication is invalid
        A-->>C: Reject, no payment dispatch
    end
    A->>P: Accepted channel request and business context
    P--)T: Redacted technical observations asynchronously throughout processing
    P->>P: Validate supported input, prior reference and resolved payment data
    break Input, context or reference is rejected
        P-->>A: Safe rejection, no dispatch
        A-->>C: Rejected request, not an invented issuer decline
    end
    P->>DB: Resolve business key or explicit original reference
    DB-->>P: Existing operation or eligible new instruction
    break Existing matching operation is replayed
        P-->>A: Original reference and latest journal-known result or uncertainty
        A-->>C: Replay only, no new financial instruction
    end
    P->>DB: Atomic CLAIMED_NOT_SENT plus critical consultable event
    DB-->>P: Commit result
    break Claim commit is failed or unreadable
        P-->>A: Truthful not-dispatched or unavailable state
        A-->>C: No automatic payment retry
    end
    P->>DB: Atomic POSSIBLE_SEND plus critical consultable event
    DB-->>P: Send-gate commit result
    break Send gate is not durably confirmed
        P-->>A: Truthful unsent or uncertain state from available evidence
        A-->>C: No automatic payment retry
    end
    P->>S: ONE financial invocation: private ISO8583 over selected HTTPS boundary
    Note over P,S: Service identity and response evidence controls apply, IP allowlist alone is not authentication
    alt Explicit network rejection before issuer forwarding
        S-->>P: Verified network rejection, no issuer decision
    else Instruction is forwarded to issuer
        S->>I: Simulated issuer authorization instruction
        I-->>S: Issuer decision when available
        S-->>P: Correlated reply, or missing/invalid/late response
    end
    alt Verified correlated issuer decision or explicit rejection is received
        P->>DB: Atomic verified receipt, business version and critical event
        DB-->>P: Evidence commit result
    else No valid timely confirmation
        P->>DB: Record conservative uncertainty and critical event when persistence is available
        DB-->>P: Commit result or persistence fault
    end
    P-->>A: Confirmed result only if durably admitted, otherwise truthful uncertainty
    A-->>C: Outcome, actual admitted transactionId and observation status
    C-->>D: Keep payment result separate from observation completeness
    Note over P,DB: Critical events are stored once and queryable, required persistence precedes dispatch
    Note over C,DB: WebSocket/notifier failure does not block this HTTP flow when required storage is healthy
    Note over C,T: Common task hooks are transversal to every implemented/future flow, lost intermediate tasks remain gaps
